# Canonical site origin (no trailing slash). Required for production
# builds — og:image, twitter:image, and og:url need absolute URLs or
# social crawlers (FB / X / LinkedIn / Slack / Discord / KakaoTalk)
# silently fail the preview, so `pnpm build` fails without it. For local
# builds copy this file to `.env.production.local` (builds only; `.env.local`
# also reaches `pnpm dev`), or set the variable in your deploy environment.
#
# The service-detail VIEW-COUNT BADGE (hits.sh) also derives from this — it
# counts under this URL's host. Empty (tests, or a dev server with no value)
# → the badge is hidden; a production build always has a value.
# PRIVACY: when set, each detail-page visit requests an SVG from hits.sh,
# which sends the visitor's IP to that third party. The placeholder below
# counts as set: a site built with it requests hits.sh for that host.
# (This site deploys to https://www.getdesign.kr — set that in your deploy env.)
VITE_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.example
